A||||3||FIEROCIOUS||New engine in and running but......?||||5||
Z||000000||FIEROCIOUS||07-19-2000||02:38 AM||||I've recently built a new engine installed it, started it (started right away)and broke in the Crane cam and lifters. <P>I followed the Chilton, Haynes, and How to rebuild your 60 V6 engine manuals by setting lash 1 1/2 turns after pushrod tightens slightly. <P>I am still hearing valve tappet noise I even took the cover off and tighten them one half turn more to no avail.<P>I also have roller rockers and thought this may be what I am hearing? On all my other cars I've used roller rockers on were quiet is this a 2.8 trait? Or do I still need to adjust them? <P>Any one have an engine apart? Approx how many threads from the tip of the rocker stud does the top of the lock nut sit? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||87GTZ34||07-19-2000||07:18 PM||||This may sound like a silly question but... is the noise you're hearing possibly the injectors?  I would think if you over tighten the rockers noises should certainly change if not go away.  As a test, go the other other way (loosen the rocker) to see if a different noise appears.<P>------------------<BR>87GTZ34||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||07-19-2000||07:38 PM||||Hi,<BR> I was thinking you could have gotten dirt in one of the lifters during assembly which would cause a noise, but from your description, they are all noisey. Am I correct? The lifters are hydraulic, so they do dot need to be adjusted to an exact spot. When you tighten them 1.5 turns past zero lash, you are setting them to the middle of their operating range. You could probably go a full turn in or out, and it wouldn't make any difference. So, what I am saying is that it's most likely not an adjustment problem as long as you adjusted each one with the engine rotated to the correct location, and if not, the engine wouldn't run well or at all.<P> It could well be the type of lifters you chose, I am not familiar with them. Maybe someone else has experience with Crane roller lifters.<P>Jon Lagler<P>------------------<BR>'86 GT 3800<BR>'87 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||FIEROCIOUS||07-19-2000||09:12 PM||||I've been doing this long enough I should have known better! If it was someone elses car I would have thought of it right away!<BR>My car is rather noisy (exhaust) and made it hard to disern were the noise was comeing from. After hot lashing the lifters (ruined the looks of my headers in the process) I realized it may be the accessories causeing the noise. Sure enough it was the altenator clicking! lesson learned?||||reg||1
